 "speed": 0.9,
 "text": "Your agent says it booked the cheapest flight. How do you know it got there the right way? Grade only the answer, and the agent is a black box. When it breaks, you can't see where. So record the whole run. An agent works in a loop. The reasoning layer, the LLM, makes a plan and picks a tool. The action layer calls the tool, and the result goes back to reason again, until the task is done. Each layer fails in its own way. Reasoning fails with a bad plan, with steps missing or out of order. Or a good plan the agent doesn't follow. So score both: plan quality, and plan adherence. Action fails at the tools. The wrong tool, like a calculator when it needed search. Or the right tool with wrong arguments: a city, when the tool wants a full location. Score that one decision: tool correctness, and argument correctness. That gives three scopes. End to end grades only the final output. Trajectory reads the whole ordered trace. Did it finish the task, without wasted steps? And component grades a single span, like the call that picked the tool. In development, run all of it on a fixed set of goldens, and compare each version. In production, catch the runs that fail, and add each one to the set. That's how you find exactly where it broke.",
